    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst Stuðningur \u003e Hugbúnaður og Eiginleikar",
    "content": "Þessi grein fjallar um nýju lykilmælinga gagnakassann sem kynntur var í útgáfu 10.0. Þó að hann hafi verið gefinn út í útgáfu 10.0 fjallar þessi grein um virkni sem er tiltæk í 10.2 sem gæti verið frábrugðin eldri útgáfum.\nTiltækt í útgáfu: 10.2 og nýrri.\nÁ við um: Motion Catalyst\nNauðsynleg vélbúnaður: Kraftplata(r) / Motion Plate / Dual Motion Plate.\nHugbúnaðarleyfi sem styður lykilmælingar.\nWhat version do I have?\nWhat are key metrics? The key metrics are derived from force data and analysis is performed on this data.\nDifferent activities have different key metrics, and not all activities have the same amount of key metrics available.\nWhat activities are key metrics available for? Key metrics are available for the following activities in Motion Catalyst:\nCounter Movement Jump\nDynamic Balance\nIsometric Mid-Thigh Pull\nPlyo-push up\nPush Up\nRepeated Hops\nStatic Balance\nSquat Jump\nUpper Body Plank\nWe are looking to expand this list and support other sports in the future such as golf \u0026 baseball.\nThe Key Metrics data box Key metrics is a new databox that shows key values from valuable points in an activity.\nIt’s possible to customize which key metrics are shown by selecting each “tile” and selecting from the key metrics drop-down menu. These selections will be remembered for the next recording you open, similar to how it remembers which databox is shown.\nPresentation options It’s possible to change the layout of the Key Metrics databox from 4, 6 or 8 metrics.\nReducing the amount of metrics can be helpful to reduce clutter and improve visibility.\nExport all key metrics (TSV) The Key Metrics databox also supports exporting all of the available key metrics to a tsv (tab separated values) file directly from the databox itself.\nKey metrics are missing for this recording In some cases key metrics aren’t available for a specific activity or the recorded activity, clicking “More info” can reveal more information about why key metrics are unavailable.\nCommon causes:\nNot performing the activity properly / according to protocol.\nMoving too much before performing the activity.\nIncorrect body weight configuration.\nBad force plate calibration (try to calibrate / zero the force plates).\nImproper force plate setup.\nI don’t have the Key Metrics data box Key metrics is only available for Motion Catalyst and for a select number of activities.\nPossible causes:\nLicense doesn’t support key metrics.\nNot using Motion Catalyst / no license for Motion Catalyst.\nActivity or sport doesn’t support key metrics.\nLast updated: 2023-12-19 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Lykilmælikvarðarnir eru fengnir frá kraftgögnum og greining er framkvæmd á þessum gögnum.",
